                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr id="recipe-34" class="recipe-row-36">
            <td style="white-space: inherit; min-width: 200px;">
                                                            <a href="/ingredients/1108" class="hyperlink colorless">
                            Pectin                        </a>
                                                    
                
                                <br><small class='text-muted'>(See notes below)</small>                            </td>
            <td class=" text-right" >

                2.0000            </td>
            <td>
                <span class="badge unit-g_50ml">g/50ml</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr id="recipe-35" class="recipe-row-37">
            <td style="white-space: inherit; min-width: 200px;">
                                    Guanosine                                
                
                                <br><small class='text-muted'>(Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.)</small>                            </td>
            <td class=" text-right" >

                0.0300            </td>
            <td>
                <span class="badge unit-g_50ml">g/50ml</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr id="recipe-36" class="recipe-row-38">
            <td style="white-space: inherit; min-width: 200px;">
                                                            <a href="/ingredients/1349" class="hyperlink colorless">
                            Uracil                        </a>
                                                    
                
                                <br><small class='text-muted'>(Single stock in NNM. Autoclave and store at -20C.)</small>                            </td>
            <td class=" text-right" >

                0.1600            </td>
            <td>
                <span class="badge unit-g_50ml">g/50ml</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr id="recipe-49" class="recipe-row-39">
            <td style="white-space: inherit; min-width: 200px;">
                                    MEM 50X Amino Acids solution (Sigma)                                
                
                                <br><small class='text-muted'>(Add directly to Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids))</small>                            </td>
            <td class="amount text-right" data-volume='2.25'>

                2.2500            </td>
            <td>
                <span class="badge unit-ml">ml</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr id="recipe-50" class="recipe-row-40">
            <td style="white-space: inherit; min-width: 200px;">
                                    MEM 100X Amino Acids solution (Sigma)                                
                
                                <br><small class='text-muted'>(Add directly to Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids))</small>                            </td>
            <td class="amount text-right" data-volume='2.27'>

                2.2700            </td>
            <td>
                <span class="badge unit-ml">ml</span>
            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
            <td class="text-right">
                -            </td>
        </tr>

            <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">1</span>
                                <img src="/img/usermedia/Fig2_RSmedium_NM_GraficScheme_MediaDive.png">                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">2</span>
                                Single stock phase: Prepare the single stocks as reported above. Single stocks are prepared either in purified H<sub>2</sub>O or in the Non-Nutrient Medium (NNM) component of RS Medium (see accompanying protocol on MediaDive). Filtration is performed with a 0.22 µm pore size.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">3</span>
                                Single stock phase: Notes for Methyl cellulose: prepare the single stock in H<sub>2</sub>O. It is known that Methyl cellulose is soluble in cold water and insoluble in hot water. In order to prepare this stock, add the relative amount and shake the single stock from time to time for 20 minutes. Leave the stock in cold water overnight. Its color should be white. The day after, after autoclaving, it will result like a white solid, not liquid. Leave it at RT until it becomes liquid and transparent. Store at 4C.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">4</span>
                                Single stock phase: Notes for Pectin: prepare the single stock in H<sub>2</sub>O. To dissolve, use a hot plate heater with a magnetic stirrer for 20 minutes before autoclaving. Store at 4C.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">5</span>
                                Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 1 (Si and Fe+EDTA): add 2.27 ml each from the single stocks of Na<sub>2</sub>SiO<sub>3</sub>*5H2O, FeCl<sub>3</sub>*6H2O and Na2EDTA*2H2O. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">6</span>
                                Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 2 (NO<sub>3</sub>-PO<sub>4</sub>): add 2.27 ml each from the single stocks of NaNO<sub>3</sub>, NaH2PO<sub>4</sub>*H<sub>2</sub>O, K2HPO<sub>4</sub> and NH<sub>4</sub>Cl. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Prepare this mix fresh every time.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">7</span>
                                Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 3 (Vitamins): add 4.5 µl each from the single stocks of vitamins (Thiamine HCl (B<sub>1</sub>), Biotin (B<sub>8</sub>), Cyanocobalamin (B<sub>1</sub>2), Folic acid (Folate) (B<sub>9</sub>), Pyridoxine (B<sub>6</sub>), Riboflavin (B<sub>2</sub>), Niacin (B<sub>3</sub>), D-pantothenate acid hemicalcium salt (B<sub>5</sub>), Myo-Inositol (B<sub>7</sub>) and 4-Aminobenzoic acid). Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C.                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">8</span>
                                Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids): add 2.25 ml from the MEM 50X Amino Acids solution from Sigma and 2.27 ml from the MEM 100X Amino Acids solution from Sigma. Add 2.27 ml of the single stock of Glutamine. Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter via syringe through a 0.22 µm pore size. Store at 4C.

NOTES: The MEM 50X AA solution contains Arginine (6.32 g/L), Cysteine HCl (1.56 g/L), Histidine (2.10 g/L), L-Isoleucine (2.63 g/L), L-Leucine (2.62 g/L), Lysine HCl (3.63 g/L), L-Methionine (0.76 g/L), L-Phenylalanine (1.65 g/L), L-Threonine (2.38 g/L), L-Tryptophan (0.51 g/L), L-Tyrosine (1.80 g/L) and L-Valine (2.34 g/L). 
The MEM 100X AA solution contains L-Alanine (0.89 g/L), Glycine (0.75 g/L), L-Proline (1.15 g/L), L-Asparagine*H<sub>2</sub>O (1.50 g/L), Aspartate (1.33 g/L), Glutamate (1.47 g/L), Serine (1.05 g/L).                            </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">9</span>
                                Mix solutions phase: Mix solution 5 (Carbon Sources): add 45 µl of Glycerol from Sigma (1.26 g/mL). Add 2.27 ml of each carbon source (Sodium pyruvate, D-glucose, N-acetyI-D-glucosamine, D-ribose, Sodium succinate, y-aminobutyric acid, Sodium acetate, Decanoic acid, L-arabinose, L-rhamnose, Fucose, L-mannose, Galactose, Xylan, Sodium alginate, Methyl-cellulose, Pectin, Guanosine and Uracil). Fill to 50 ml with NNM. Filter through a 0.22 µm pore size by using the vacuum filter (not by syringe) because the solution is viscous. Store at 4C.                             </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">10</span>
                                Final phase: Combine 4 ml of Mix solution 1 (Si and Fe+EDTA), 30 ml from Mix solution 2 (NO<sub>3</sub>-PO<sub>4</sub>), 10.7 ml from Mix solution 3 (Vitamins), 10.9 ml of Mix solution 4 (Amino Acids) and 10.7 ml of Mix solution 5 (Carbon sources). Fill to 150 ml with NNM. Filter through a 0.22 µm pore size by using a vacuum filter. Store Nutrient Medium 1.0 (NM 1.0) component at 4C.                             </td>
        </tr>
                <tr class="step-row">
            <td colspan="6" class="" style="white-space: inherit; max-width: 100%;">
                                    <span class="step-number">11</span>
                                Acknowledgements: We would like to thank Ben Temperton (University of Exteter) for fundamental advice and ideas in the creation of RS medium.                            </td>
        </tr>
                            </table>
                </div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>




</div>

</div>
<div class="col-lg-5">

    <div class="content mt-0">
        
        <h3 id="title-metadata" class="mt-md-0">
            Metadata        </h3>

        <table class="table small" id="metadata-box">
            
                            <tr>
                    <td>Creator:</td>
                    <td>
                        Cristiana Sigona                        
                    </td>
                </tr>
                                    <tr>
                        <td>Author(s):</td>

                        <td>
                                                            <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9238-5571" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><i class="ph ph-orcid"></i></a>
                            
                            Cristiana Sigona, Daniel J. Richter                        </td>
                    </tr>

                                <tr>
                    <td>Published:</td>
                    <td>
                                                    30.06.23                                            </td>
                </tr>
            
            <tr>
                <td>Last modified:</td>
                <td>
                    07.10.25                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Source:</td>
                <td>
                                            <span>Media<em>Dive</em>: public</span>
                                    </td>
            </tr>
            
            
            <tr>
                <td>Medium type:</td>
                <td>
                    Complex medium                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Final pH:</td>
                <td>
                    <span id="pH-value">7</span>
                </td>
            </tr>
                            <tr>
                    <td>Equipment needed:</td>
                    <td>
                        Autoclave, Autoclavable bottles, 0.22 µm vaccum filters, 0.22 µm syringe filters, 50 ml conical tubes                    </td>
                </tr>
                                                    <tr>
                    <td colspan="2">
                        Description:
                        <br>
                        <p id="description">The RS medium is a fully defined medium designed for growing diverse marine protists. RS medium presents a natural buffer system with a pH of ~7 and a salinity of 3,3%. It includes two components: the Non-Nutrient Medium (NNM) and the Nutrient Medium 1.0 (NM 1.0). Here we show the preparation of the NM 1.0</p>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                                        <tr class="d-none d-sm-table-row">
                    <td colspan="2">
                                                <button class="btn" onclick="showQR('https%3A%2F%2Fmediadive.dsmz.de%2Fmedium%2FP5')" id="qrcode">
                            <i class="ph ph-qr-code ph-lg mr-10 ph-fw"></i>
                            Show QR code for mobile                        </button>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                <tr class="d-none d-sm-table-row">
                    <td colspan="2">
                        <a href="/medium-builder?medium=P5" class="btn" id="medium-builder">
                            <!-- <i class="ph ph-note-pencil ph-lg mr-10"></i> -->
                            <i class="ph ph-flask-pen ph-lg mr-5 ph-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            Edit in Medium builder                        </a>
                    </td>
                </tr>
                    </table>

        

